    "created_at": "2016-04-14T12:54:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-14T12:54:47Z",
    "body": "In https://codereview.chromium.org/1881733004/ (by @wolenetz) it looks like implementation-wise it's more straightforward to just check if it's a blob: URL and not care whether it corresponds to an object at that point.\n\nDepending on how one correctly gets from a blob: URL to an actual object (@annevk?) it might make more sense to keep blob: URLs in the remote branch and instead just skip the preload check, which is what the Chromium CL does.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
